    <h2>1. Problem Statement</h2>
    <p>
        Despite advancements in assistive technology, most urban infrastructures remain static. For individuals with disabilities, navigating complex environments—from public transit to bustling shopping districts—remains a source of constant stress and physical limitation. Current solutions are often reactive rather than proactive, failing to anticipate the needs of the user in real-time.
    </p>

